      "writtenOn": "2021-09-18T04:20:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Interestingly a standard use case for available is to only wait for it once, but caps can be sent any number of times.\n• You could decide to only support the first one, but then you should throw in onCapabilitiesChanged if already received. Unfortunately this is not very realistic since is CTS onCapabilitiesChanged will be called multiple times in practice.\n• You could only accept one call to waitForCapabilitiesChanged and throw on the second call. It\u0027s not very nice to callers but at least it\u0027s easy to do\n• Or you could actually have this be cyclic, but this is a lot harder to implement. You\u0027ll need a lock, and/or a CyclicBarrier.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 756,
        "startChar": 35,
        "endLine": 756,
        "endChar": 61
      },
